<p>A humanitarian flotilla is sailing to Cuba with supplies as the island struggles through a severe energy crisis. Organizers are framing the mission as both practical relief and a show of solidarity. At the same time, coverage makes clear that outside support for Cuba remains politically contested.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/46Ui6r95M9oFs6aV8ZBxd7qgnz6NoEZ6q5J9igt3ZNE2C1rKmYp1xe3Y4fqXZQhPxhS0WJgnjmo2wGh4ujx1DUYn6LiJ2OnZAh6C1FMkeyQnGtFCZJVZ7i8gCaOE082YuDHIzpZhN6WPo4WwmExfUprWCsqzTm7LuHxQOC2n0WoEK4o_HDnsydZMhUTtgubkr2iyUZcWVJU' alt='People watching the sunset in Havana on Monday during a blackout.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mission identity: The New York Times said the convoy is called “Nuestra América,” a name that underscores the trip’s regional-solidarity message.</li><li>Mexico launch point: Al Jazeera reported that the flotilla set sail from Mexico, which served as the staging ground for the humanitarian mission.</li><li>Fuel squeeze: Al Jazeera described Cuba’s situation as a tightening US fuel blockade, showing why energy access is at the heart of the emergency.</li><li>Arrival phase: ABC News reported that aid and delegates had started arriving in Cuba, signaling a shift from transit to on-the-ground delivery.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Convoy organizers: Organizers described the “Nuestra América” mission as a humanitarian convoy carrying critical supplies to Cuba during the island’s energy crisis. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/americas/cuba-fuel-blockade-aid-convoy.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Some Cuban exiles: Some Cuban exiles saw the convoy with suspicion, reflecting broader distrust over how aid to Cuba can intersect with politics and sanctions debates. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/americas/cuba-fuel-blockade-aid-convoy.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Solidarity delegates: Delegates from dozens of countries and organizations joined the caravan as a show of solidarity, signaling support for humanitarian assistance despite the deepening energy strain. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/tons-aid-flows-cuba-humanitarian-convoy-arrives-struggling-131270968'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/americas/cuba-fuel-blockade-aid-convoy.html'>Aid Ship Departs for Cuba as Island Grapples With a Fuel Blockade</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/21/aid-flotilla-for-cuba-sets-sail-from-mexico'>Aid flotilla for Cuba sets sail from Mexico</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/tons-aid-flows-cuba-humanitarian-convoy-arrives-struggling-131270968'>Tons of aid flows into Cuba as humanitarian convoy arrives on the struggling island</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>